🧠 What is Intrinsic Lock?
-In Java, every object automatically has an intrinsic lock (or monitor lock)
associated to it.
-The moment a thread enters the synchronized block or method,
it gets the lock for the object, and then no other thread is
allowed to enter the synchronized block or method for that object until
  the lock is released.

-intrinsic lock=built in lock that every java object has
-it is alos called as:
monitor lock or object lock
👉 “It is the internal lock associated with every object in Java,
 which is used by synchronized methods and blocks to
ensure only one thread executes critical section at a time.”

👉 Intrinsic lock = object-level lock automatically used by synchronized
