4. Volatile Keyword
👉 volatile is used for variables in multithreading
👉 It ensures:
latest value is always visible to all threads

🧠 Problem (without volatile)
👉 Each thread has its own cache memory
Thread1 → has its copy
Thread2 → has its copy
👉 If one thread updates value:
❌ Other thread may NOT see it
❌ Uses old value → wrong result
👉 “In this example, volatile ensures that when the main thread updates the running flag,
 the worker thread immediately sees the change and stops execution.”

 🧠 When volatile FAILS
 👉 volatile only gives:
 ✔ Visibility
 ❌ NOT thread safety
 ❌ NOT atomicity

 “Volatile ensures visibility but does not guarantee atomicity.
  For example, increment operations like count++ are not atomic,
  so multiple threads can
 cause inconsistent results even if the variable is volatile.”

